    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0873" n="753" xml:id="pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.34/181: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-22T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1922—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 22—10:03
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>279. Having communicated to Chinese Foreign Office text of memorandum contained
                    in Department’s May 4, 2 p.m., to Tokio,<anchor n="96" xml:id="d537-f1"/> Under
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs transmits from Minister of Marine communication
                    which after reciting facts of the case ends, “having now received statement of
                    American Minister that at present Bethlehem Steel Corporation and the United
                    States Government cannot undertake to carry out the contract, therefore previous
                    discussions should be entirely canceled and the matter ended. It is [requested]
                    that you inform American Minister to take the necessary action in the premises.”
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs says, “I have the honor to transmit the above to
                    you for your information.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
